WEBVTT


00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.500
Downloaded @ subs4free.club

﻿1

00:00:43.054 --> 00:00:48.054
Subtitles by explosiveskull
@ subs4free.info


00:01:13.656 --> 00:01:15.032
Look what I found.


00:01:17.618 --> 00:01:18.536
Candy!


00:01:19.537 --> 00:01:21.414
Gunnery Sergeant Gorski.


00:01:22.748 --> 00:01:24.166
Yes, ma'am?


00:01:25.209 --> 00:01:28.045
I'm confident my daughter
will appreciate some female company.


00:01:28.129 --> 00:01:30.548
- Yes, ma'am.
- Shall we proceed, Mr. Laughlin?


00:01:32.383 --> 00:01:34.218
Come on, Nira. Let's get comfy.


00:01:35.928 --> 00:01:37.555
<i>Secure VIP's daughter
in Eagle Three.</i>


00:01:37.638 --> 00:01:38.681
Copy that, Chief.


00:01:39.682 --> 00:01:42.143
Mr. Collins,
let's go over the presentation.


00:01:42.226 --> 00:01:43.894
This is so pretty.


00:01:43.978 --> 00:01:47.023
<i>All teams, this is Six.
Radio check. Over.</i>


00:01:47.106 --> 00:01:48.858
<i>Eagle One, Roger. Out.</i>


00:01:48.941 --> 00:01:50.568
<i>Eagle Two, Roger. Out.</i>


00:01:50.651 --> 00:01:52.236
<i>Eagle Three, Roger. Out.</i>


00:01:53.487 --> 00:01:55.364
<i>Eagle Four, Roger. Out.</i>


00:01:55.448 --> 00:01:58.951
<i>Eagle Nine, this is Eagle Six.
Radio check, over.</i>


00:02:54.674 --> 00:02:57.968
How come there's so many cars
with us today?


00:02:58.052 --> 00:03:00.221
To make sure you and your mommy
are super safe.


00:03:01.222 --> 00:03:02.390
Okay.


00:03:04.850 --> 00:03:07.186
Can I have another piece of candy?


00:03:07.269 --> 00:03:09.271
- You're gonna get me in trouble.
- Yes.


00:03:11.732 --> 00:03:12.817
All right, just one.


00:03:14.276 --> 00:03:15.111
Thank you.


00:03:21.033 --> 00:03:23.035
We may have a situation.


00:03:23.119 --> 00:03:24.328
<i>Grouping in the woods
at three o'clock.</i>


00:03:28.874 --> 00:03:30.126
Yeah, that's an all clear.


00:03:42.304 --> 00:03:43.305
Holy... No!


00:03:56.235 --> 00:03:57.528
Johnson, take the lead!
Go, go, go!


00:04:21.469 --> 00:04:23.512
- Ali?
- Nothing is gonna happen to you, okay?


00:04:23.596 --> 00:04:25.014
Nothing is gonna happen to you.


00:04:26.682 --> 00:04:28.184
Is Nira all right?


00:04:33.689 --> 00:04:35.065
Back it up! Back it up! Back it up!


00:05:00.090 --> 00:05:01.509
All right, sweetie.


00:05:01.592 --> 00:05:03.677
Sweetie, I need you to sit here
and stay low, okay?


00:05:28.369 --> 00:05:29.662
Come on. Let's go!


00:05:32.790 --> 00:05:34.083
- Mommy!
- It's okay.


00:06:39.982 --> 00:06:43.193
- So when'd you get back?
- To New York?


00:06:43.277 --> 00:06:44.528
About a week.


00:06:46.155 --> 00:06:47.615
Do you have a place to stay?


00:06:49.450 --> 00:06:50.784
What about a job?


00:06:51.785 --> 00:06:52.995
Hmm.


00:06:53.078 --> 00:06:55.331
It wasn't exactly a parade
welcoming me home.


00:06:57.458 --> 00:06:59.877
Well, I missed you at the funeral.


00:07:02.504 --> 00:07:03.881
They wouldn't let me go.


00:07:05.090 --> 00:07:06.508
What, for your sister?


00:07:06.592 --> 00:07:08.928
<i>Non sibi sed patriae.</i>


00:07:09.011 --> 00:07:13.349
- Not self, but country and all that.
- That's Navy, not us.


00:07:14.475 --> 00:07:16.143
It seemed to make sense at the time.


00:07:19.480 --> 00:07:22.066
You know, the kids would benefit from
having their aunt around.


00:07:24.151 --> 00:07:25.694
Any interest in seeing them?


00:07:27.488 --> 00:07:28.322
Jon?


00:07:35.204 --> 00:07:36.413
Okay then.


00:07:38.540 --> 00:07:42.169
There's an opening at the apartment
building where I'm working.


00:07:42.252 --> 00:07:43.796
It's not much, but it's something.


00:07:45.005 --> 00:07:46.590
They're doing major renovations.


00:07:46.674 --> 00:07:49.927
You get the job,
hardly anybody will be there.


00:07:51.428 --> 00:07:53.222
Not quite as exciting
as where you've been.


00:08:01.939 --> 00:08:05.901
You know, when we fought in Vietnam,
we saw a lot of things.


00:08:07.778 --> 00:08:11.156
After the war, the only people who really
understood what we went through...


00:08:12.282 --> 00:08:13.701
were the other soldiers.


00:08:15.077 --> 00:08:16.912
There's groups you can talk to.


00:08:21.917 --> 00:08:23.752
Don't worry. I'm fine.


00:08:25.129 --> 00:08:26.630
I'll check out this job.


00:08:31.343 --> 00:08:32.845
I missed you, Uncle Pat.


00:10:04.311 --> 00:10:06.355
I owe you a couple of Mets tickets.


00:10:06.438 --> 00:10:08.440
Not until they got a team worth watching.


00:10:09.733 --> 00:10:12.194
Hey, so where do I find Borz Blasevic?


00:10:12.277 --> 00:10:15.114
In the locker room.
Take the elevator down to the basement,


00:10:15.197 --> 00:10:17.116
go left through the fire doors.
You'll see it.


00:10:17.199 --> 00:10:18.784
And don't tell him we're related.


00:10:18.867 --> 00:10:21.829
- He'll go easier on you.
- All right.


00:10:25.916 --> 00:10:27.000
Hey, Uncle Pat.


00:10:28.001 --> 00:10:28.836
Thanks.


00:10:36.635 --> 00:10:38.011
- Hi.
- Hi.


00:10:39.012 --> 00:10:40.806
- You're Gorski?
- Yes, Sir.


00:10:40.889 --> 00:10:42.057
Pat told me you were coming.


00:10:43.267 --> 00:10:44.518
He's a nice guy.


00:10:46.228 --> 00:10:48.105
- Don't you think?
- Yes, Sir.


00:10:48.188 --> 00:10:49.982
You can put your stuff...


00:10:51.441 --> 00:10:52.484
here.


00:10:53.610 --> 00:10:55.320
Sorry about this.
We're all unisex here.


00:11:00.534 --> 00:11:02.911
This is what I love about Rachmaninoff.


00:11:04.663 --> 00:11:06.456
He's so unexpected.


00:11:06.540 --> 00:11:08.458
I feel the same way about Dylan.


00:11:08.542 --> 00:11:10.669
- Thomas?
- Bob.


00:11:12.087 --> 00:11:14.673
You're not a fan
of classical work, are you?


00:11:14.756 --> 00:11:16.175
Not exactly, sir.


00:11:17.885 --> 00:11:19.386
You can cut the "sir" crap.


00:11:20.512 --> 00:11:22.097
We have enough kissing up
to do here already.


00:11:22.181 --> 00:11:23.348
We don't have to do it to each other.


00:11:25.100 --> 00:11:27.811
We'll use the next two days
to get you acclimated.


00:11:27.895 --> 00:11:29.771
You get the Easter weekend off.


00:11:29.855 --> 00:11:32.107
Everyone will be out of the building,
SO you won't miss much.


00:11:32.191 --> 00:11:34.693
You come back to work on Monday.


00:11:34.776 --> 00:11:38.405
There will be more babysitting
The Carrington while it gets a facelift.


00:11:38.488 --> 00:11:40.866
Think you can handle that?


00:11:40.949 --> 00:11:42.034
I'll do my best, sir.


00:11:43.035 --> 00:11:43.911
Good.


00:11:48.665 --> 00:11:50.584
- Let's go, let's go!
- Holiday!


00:11:52.544 --> 00:11:54.963
Hey!


00:11:55.047 --> 00:11:57.925
I may be old-fashioned,
but a woman doorman?


00:11:58.008 --> 00:12:01.053
We're trying to modernize our image
at The Carrington, sir. I'm sorry.


00:12:06.475 --> 00:12:08.143
Here, let me help you with those.


00:12:08.227 --> 00:12:10.604
- Oh, no. I got them.
- I insist, I insist.


00:12:10.687 --> 00:12:12.522
Thank you.


00:12:12.606 --> 00:12:14.483
<i>You're not moving
during the remodeling?</i>


00:12:14.566 --> 00:12:18.695
Borz was kind enough
to arrange an exception for us.


00:12:18.779 --> 00:12:21.698
Poor Bernard had a stroke
seven years ago.


00:12:22.908 --> 00:12:25.953
You know how old fogies
feel about change.


00:12:26.036 --> 00:12:28.038
Old fogies. Come on, you're not that old.


00:12:28.121 --> 00:12:31.375
You're kind.


00:12:31.458 --> 00:12:34.670
A liar, but kind nevertheless.


00:12:38.757 --> 00:12:41.510
Oh, that was very helpful, dear.


00:12:43.887 --> 00:12:46.974
You know, your sister never stopped
talking about you.


00:12:48.058 --> 00:12:49.643
- Now I know why.
- Wait.


00:12:50.644 --> 00:12:52.479
How do you know my sister?


00:12:52.562 --> 00:12:54.731
Well, you're Ali, right?


00:12:54.815 --> 00:12:57.109
Your sister and family
lived in the building.


00:12:57.192 --> 00:12:59.194
Her husband and kids still do.


00:13:00.487 --> 00:13:01.697
Where is he?


00:13:02.698 --> 00:13:03.532
10C.


00:13:04.533 --> 00:13:08.203
Oh, lovely family,
but tragic what they've lived through.


00:13:10.914 --> 00:13:13.041
Have a happy Easter.


00:13:21.842 --> 00:13:23.427
Why didn't you tell me?


00:13:24.845 --> 00:13:26.430
Well, I was gonna...


00:13:26.513 --> 00:13:28.974
You know, I thought being
close to family might...


00:13:31.560 --> 00:13:33.729
might be, you know...


00:13:35.856 --> 00:13:37.149
nice.


00:13:39.276 --> 00:13:41.903
- Max, get the door.
- I'm busy.


00:13:41.987 --> 00:13:45.198
Max, I swear to God,
I'm gonna throw that game out the window.


00:13:48.285 --> 00:13:50.996
- What?
- Is your father home by any chance?


00:13:51.079 --> 00:13:52.080
It's for you.


00:13:53.582 --> 00:13:55.334
Well, who is it? I'm working.


00:14:01.757 --> 00:14:05.093
- Ali.
- What the hell is going on?


00:14:05.177 --> 00:14:07.429
- You tell me. Are you working here?
- Yeah.


00:14:07.512 --> 00:14:09.431
And that has nothing to do with you?


00:14:10.849 --> 00:14:12.017
No.


00:14:12.100 --> 00:14:13.769
Damn it, Uncle Pat.


00:14:16.355 --> 00:14:17.981
- You want to come in?
- No.


00:14:19.274 --> 00:14:20.984
I did not ask for this.


00:14:21.068 --> 00:14:23.695
Believe me, I had no idea
you were gonna end up here.


00:14:25.072 --> 00:14:26.448
- Jasper!
- No.


00:14:26.531 --> 00:14:28.825
Jasper! Damn it.


00:14:28.909 --> 00:14:31.244
Lily, how many times? Words.


00:14:32.245 --> 00:14:34.706
We have to find him.


00:14:35.957 --> 00:14:37.876
Uh, look, I've got to get this.


00:14:37.959 --> 00:14:40.921
It's my publisher in London.
We've been missing each other all morning.


00:14:41.004 --> 00:14:43.632
Can you just... I won't be long.


00:14:46.676 --> 00:14:48.762
Do you need help?


00:14:48.845 --> 00:14:52.557
Jasper could be anywhere by now.
We need Max.


00:14:52.641 --> 00:14:54.351
- Come on!
- Oh! Okay.


00:14:56.353 --> 00:14:58.021
Max!


00:14:59.773 --> 00:15:00.941
Go away.


00:15:02.859 --> 00:15:04.694
Lily, what the hell?


00:15:04.778 --> 00:15:06.655
Jasper escaped again.
We need your help.


00:15:06.738 --> 00:15:08.031
Get out!


00:15:09.491 --> 00:15:11.576
I don't have time to look
for your stupid cat.


00:15:13.120 --> 00:15:16.456
If you don't help us, I'll tell Dad
that you're smoking marijuana again.


00:15:19.334 --> 00:15:20.794
Jasper!


00:15:21.962 --> 00:15:23.713
Jasper, come here.


00:15:23.797 --> 00:15:25.715
There's 63 apartments on ten floors,


00:15:25.799 --> 00:15:27.884
all of them open for the contractor.


00:15:28.885 --> 00:15:30.971
This is gonna take forever.


00:15:31.054 --> 00:15:33.056
Max collected all of the blueprints
for The Carrington


00:15:33.140 --> 00:15:35.934
- when he was a Boy Scout.
- Max, a Boy Scout?


00:15:37.227 --> 00:15:38.437
I can see that.


00:15:39.438 --> 00:15:40.439
Jasper?


00:15:43.984 --> 00:15:44.818
Jasper?


00:15:45.819 --> 00:15:47.362
Jasper!


00:15:47.446 --> 00:15:48.655
Where are you?


00:15:52.159 --> 00:15:53.368
Where'd your brother go?


00:15:54.369 --> 00:15:57.706
Max? Max, this isn't funny.


00:15:57.789 --> 00:15:59.666
Max, where'd you go?


00:16:00.792 --> 00:16:02.002
- Max...
- Ahh!


00:16:04.045 --> 00:16:05.422
Butt brain!


00:16:05.505 --> 00:16:07.257
Where did you even
come from anyway?


00:16:07.340 --> 00:16:10.135
A secret door.
Building's full of them.


00:16:10.218 --> 00:16:12.471
Servants used them
to get from room to room.


00:16:12.554 --> 00:16:13.555
Huh.


00:16:15.432 --> 00:16:16.850
Jasper!


00:16:18.143 --> 00:16:20.520
- What's your name anyhow?
- Ali.


00:16:21.521 --> 00:16:23.190
Aunt Ali?


00:16:23.273 --> 00:16:24.900
Mommy told us all about you.


00:16:26.193 --> 00:16:28.653
- She did?
- Yeah, you were her hero.


00:16:30.030 --> 00:16:31.656
So how do we find Jasper anyway?


00:16:31.740 --> 00:16:32.949
Jasper...


00:16:33.033 --> 00:16:34.367
Let's check the basement.


00:16:40.290 --> 00:16:42.792
That's Jasper.


00:16:44.628 --> 00:16:46.505
What's through this wall?


00:16:46.588 --> 00:16:49.925
They were building a subway tunnel
under The Carrington.


00:16:50.008 --> 00:16:52.761
Ran out of money in the '40s,
sealed it up.


00:16:54.638 --> 00:16:55.680
Jasper.


00:16:57.641 --> 00:16:58.934
Jasper!


00:16:59.976 --> 00:17:03.021
Please be okay.


00:17:03.104 --> 00:17:04.481
Max, give me your phone.


00:17:10.487 --> 00:17:11.905
There he is.


00:17:11.988 --> 00:17:14.574
- What do we do?
- Now, let's see.


00:17:24.459 --> 00:17:25.961
What's she doing?


00:17:26.044 --> 00:17:27.629
Do not try this at home.


00:17:36.680 --> 00:17:38.974
I didn't think
we'd ever see Jasper again,


00:17:39.057 --> 00:17:43.436
but then Aunt Ali dropped into the hole
like Spider-Man and saved him.


00:17:44.854 --> 00:17:46.147
- Really?
- Yep.


00:17:46.231 --> 00:17:48.858
Your aunt was always full of surprises.


00:17:48.942 --> 00:17:51.361
Right. You, go in and get
started on Mommy's mint sauce,


00:17:51.444 --> 00:17:52.988
and I'll join you in a minute.


00:17:53.071 --> 00:17:55.907
Will you come to Easter dinner tomorrow?
I'm cooking it.


00:17:57.200 --> 00:17:58.743
Lily, I would love that but...


00:17:58.827 --> 00:18:00.370
You got to eat.


00:18:03.123 --> 00:18:05.500
It'll give us a chance to reconnect.


00:18:06.501 --> 00:18:08.795
I don't want to reconnect.


00:18:10.880 --> 00:18:13.133
I'm taking the kids
back to the UK on Monday.


00:18:13.216 --> 00:18:16.886
During the construction, you'll have
the place to yourself without us.


00:18:16.970 --> 00:18:20.557
The only reason we stayed so long was Lily
wanted to make an Easter dinner here.


00:18:21.558 --> 00:18:23.143
Like her mother did.


00:18:24.978 --> 00:18:27.063
I know.


00:18:27.147 --> 00:18:29.524
We weren't really in touch, and ll...


00:18:30.525 --> 00:18:31.943
I didn't know what to say.


00:18:32.027 --> 00:18:33.653
Please, Ali?


00:19:06.102 --> 00:19:07.437
You're still here, buddy?


00:19:09.522 --> 00:19:11.983
Your shift ended over an hour ago.


00:19:12.067 --> 00:19:14.402
Don't you have an Easter feast
waiting for you somewhere?


00:19:14.486 --> 00:19:18.281
I promised Mrs. Hersch
I'd fix her microwave before I went home.


00:19:19.282 --> 00:19:20.950
That's thoughtful of you.


00:19:21.034 --> 00:19:23.411
Yeah, well, I don't want
to disappoint her.


00:19:23.495 --> 00:19:25.080
Do you wanna share a beer?


00:19:26.414 --> 00:19:29.042
- Start the celebration.
- Yeah, sure.


00:19:33.630 --> 00:19:34.881
Hey, hey, tilt the glass.


00:19:34.964 --> 00:19:37.175
You never poured a beer before?


00:19:37.258 --> 00:19:38.593
Like this?


00:19:38.677 --> 00:19:40.095
- Is that better?
- Yeah.


00:19:40.178 --> 00:19:41.680
A better tilt?


00:19:41.763 --> 00:19:43.473
So what's your plans tonight?


00:19:43.556 --> 00:19:45.517
At home. TV, bed.


00:19:45.600 --> 00:19:47.394
- No party?
- No party.


00:19:47.477 --> 00:19:49.813
Okay. Here's some beer, at least.


00:20:28.017 --> 00:20:30.019
- You're back already.
- I am.


00:20:30.103 --> 00:20:31.855
I told you to take the holiday off.


00:20:31.938 --> 00:20:34.107
The Stantons invited me for dinner.


00:20:34.190 --> 00:20:36.776
- You work fast.
- Sheer force of my personality maybe.


00:20:36.860 --> 00:20:38.278
You're staying in?


00:20:38.361 --> 00:20:40.155
Yeah. Home-cooked meal.


00:20:40.238 --> 00:20:43.658
Trust me, I would welcome any chance
to duck out, but I promised, so...


00:20:44.743 --> 00:20:46.536
Okay.


00:20:46.619 --> 00:20:48.955
You want me to save you some pie?
It's fresh from the deli.


00:20:49.038 --> 00:20:50.874
No, it's okay. I'm on a diet.


00:20:52.625 --> 00:20:53.918
Your loss.


00:20:55.545 --> 00:20:56.796
Have fun.


00:21:52.268 --> 00:21:53.728
Shall we begin?


00:22:06.699 --> 00:22:08.326
Jammer's set. Good to go.


00:22:12.705 --> 00:22:16.709
Cut it. Cut it. Cut the blue one.


00:22:16.793 --> 00:22:19.629
Let me handle it. I got it, I got it.


00:22:19.712 --> 00:22:21.381
Please. Thank you.


00:22:24.008 --> 00:22:25.385
Whoa!


00:22:27.720 --> 00:22:30.723
Whoo! Rock and roll.


00:22:36.187 --> 00:22:38.106
- What's this?
- Something I made for you.


00:22:39.524 --> 00:22:40.692
Wait, Lily, this is amazing.


00:22:40.775 --> 00:22:43.444
How did you draw this?
It looks exactly like me.


00:22:43.528 --> 00:22:45.488
I used a picture of you and Daddy.


00:22:49.367 --> 00:22:50.785
Where'd you find this?


00:22:50.869 --> 00:22:53.246
In Daddy's memory book.
Don't you like it?


00:22:54.414 --> 00:22:57.542
Yeah. No, I love it. It's amazing.
Thank you so much.


00:22:57.625 --> 00:23:01.087
I am gonna put it right up here
so that everyone can enjoy it.


00:23:01.170 --> 00:23:02.171
Do you think they'll like it?


00:23:04.173 --> 00:23:06.426
Of course.


00:23:09.304 --> 00:23:12.348
Speaking of everyone,
where is your father?


00:23:12.432 --> 00:23:14.642
- He's busy.
- He's always busy.


00:23:18.897 --> 00:23:20.899
Your mommy told me a story.


00:23:20.982 --> 00:23:22.692
Do you know what water wings are?


00:23:23.860 --> 00:23:26.195
Daddy made me wear them
when I learned to swim.


00:23:26.279 --> 00:23:27.739
It's so frustrating.


00:23:29.365 --> 00:23:31.826
Can you imagine wearing them
every single day?


00:23:31.910 --> 00:23:34.412
I wouldn't cope. I'd die.


00:23:34.495 --> 00:23:37.540
What if I told you that your daddy
used to wear them


00:23:37.624 --> 00:23:39.959
every single time he left the house?


00:23:40.043 --> 00:23:41.961
- You're kidding.
- It's true.


00:23:42.045 --> 00:23:45.381
Your grandma lived in a house
with a really big lake,


00:23:45.465 --> 00:23:49.427
so every time your daddy wanted to go out
and play, she made him wear them.


00:23:50.595 --> 00:23:52.096
You're kidding!


00:23:52.180 --> 00:23:56.100
So, every time you get a little
mad at your dad, just remember...


00:23:56.184 --> 00:23:58.853
- water wings.
- Water wings.


00:23:58.937 --> 00:24:00.021
Mm-hmm.


00:24:00.104 --> 00:24:02.607
Sorry, I had a deadline.


00:24:02.690 --> 00:24:04.692
Finally got the publisher off my back.


00:24:06.319 --> 00:24:07.403
Okay.


00:24:08.738 --> 00:24:10.073
What are you doing?


00:24:11.074 --> 00:24:12.033
Shh.


00:24:12.116 --> 00:24:13.242
Help your sister.


00:24:19.248 --> 00:24:20.291
Did I miss something?


00:24:20.375 --> 00:24:22.335
What? No.
Miss something? Here?


00:24:22.418 --> 00:24:24.212
- Nothing at all.
- There's nothing to miss.


00:24:24.295 --> 00:24:26.756
- Just talking about vegetables.
- Love vegetables.


00:24:26.839 --> 00:24:27.840
- Yeah.
- Yeah.


00:24:28.925 --> 00:24:30.176
All right.


00:24:35.431 --> 00:24:37.850
That must be Pat to fix the microwave.


00:24:41.104 --> 00:24:42.522
Oh, Borz!


00:24:42.605 --> 00:24:44.565
- Happy Easter.
- Happy Easter.


00:24:44.649 --> 00:24:46.025
What can I do for you?


00:24:46.109 --> 00:24:48.319
- You have a visitor.
- I wasn't expecting one.


00:24:48.403 --> 00:24:50.279
It's an old friend of your husband.


00:24:50.363 --> 00:24:52.573
A friend of Bernard's?


00:24:52.657 --> 00:24:53.658
Good evening.


00:24:53.741 --> 00:24:55.618
- Oh!
- My name is Victor Dubois.


00:24:55.702 --> 00:25:00.289
I happen to be in town briefly
for the holiday and wanted to stop by.


00:25:00.373 --> 00:25:02.792
I hope this is not too much
of an inconvenience.


00:25:02.875 --> 00:25:04.961
Oh, of course not!


00:25:05.044 --> 00:25:06.879
Oh, come in, come in.


00:25:06.963 --> 00:25:09.382
Can I get you anything? Some tea?


00:25:09.465 --> 00:25:12.844
- We have plenty of food.
- Some tea would be delightful.


00:25:15.763 --> 00:25:16.764
My old friend.


00:25:17.765 --> 00:25:20.560
Bernard hardly says a word
since the stroke.


00:25:20.643 --> 00:25:23.688
The doctors say it triggered
akinetic mutism.


00:25:24.981 --> 00:25:26.899
Now Mr. Dubois,


00:25:26.983 --> 00:25:29.819
how do you know my husband?


00:25:29.902 --> 00:25:32.697
We worked together in Berlin
over 30 years ago.


00:25:34.115 --> 00:25:36.909
My Bernard?


00:25:36.993 --> 00:25:38.870
Oh, no, that's not possible.


00:25:38.953 --> 00:25:42.040
He went by the name
of Erich Dreischler then.


00:25:42.123 --> 00:25:45.960
- I'm afraid you have the wrong person.
- I'm afraid not.


00:25:46.961 --> 00:25:48.212
Erich.


00:25:54.385 --> 00:25:57.138
Mr. Dubois, my husband
doesn't speak French.


00:25:57.221 --> 00:26:00.933
- He's never even been to Europe.
- Erich?


00:26:04.103 --> 00:26:06.147
Borz? What is this about?


00:26:06.230 --> 00:26:09.150
Sit down. Sit down.


00:26:11.110 --> 00:26:13.654
It seems there's a lot you don't know
about your husband, Mrs. Hersch.


00:26:16.741 --> 00:26:20.703
I can't wait until dinner.
I'm starving.


00:26:22.663 --> 00:26:24.999
So, what was it like over there?


00:26:26.292 --> 00:26:28.878
It was... it was great.


00:26:28.961 --> 00:26:30.254
Did you kill anyone?


00:26:30.338 --> 00:26:33.716
Max, don't be an imbecile.
That's totally out of line.


00:26:35.843 --> 00:26:38.888
No, it's... it's fine.


00:26:38.971 --> 00:26:40.848
Yeah. Yes, I did.


00:26:42.058 --> 00:26:43.017
Cool.


00:26:44.018 --> 00:26:45.186
More wine?


00:26:46.562 --> 00:26:48.356
Yeah. Yeah, of course.


00:26:48.439 --> 00:26:49.774
Just open another bottle.


00:26:52.193 --> 00:26:56.030
I just wish everything could go back
to the way it was before Mommy died.


00:26:57.782 --> 00:27:01.077
So, uh, how long do these go in for?


00:27:01.160 --> 00:27:03.162
About 50 minutes.


00:27:03.246 --> 00:27:06.249
They'll be... fine when you take them out.


00:27:08.084 --> 00:27:10.503
Dreischler, I know everything.


00:27:20.930 --> 00:27:24.100
I told you, we don't know anything.


00:27:24.183 --> 00:27:25.184
Would you like some help?


00:27:27.603 --> 00:27:28.437
Not yet.


00:27:29.438 --> 00:27:30.523
Erich.


00:27:40.116 --> 00:27:41.367
What about now?


00:27:43.202 --> 00:27:44.495
Refresh his memory.


00:27:55.173 --> 00:27:56.424
He's a tough old guy.


00:27:56.507 --> 00:27:58.009
He's had a stroke.


00:27:58.092 --> 00:27:59.969
- Sit down. Sit down!
- He can't feel a thing


00:28:00.052 --> 00:28:01.804
on that side of his body.


00:28:04.223 --> 00:28:05.725
Try the other side.


00:28:10.980 --> 00:28:12.148
That's better.


00:28:15.776 --> 00:28:16.903
Dubois.


00:28:17.904 --> 00:28:20.239
Welcome back, <i>Herr</i> Dreischler.


00:28:26.078 --> 00:28:27.788
In the wall.


00:28:27.872 --> 00:28:29.457
Which wall? Point to it.


00:28:34.795 --> 00:28:35.755
Here.


00:28:39.634 --> 00:28:41.135
Oh, no, no, no.


00:28:42.428 --> 00:28:43.679
Here.


00:28:46.974 --> 00:28:48.392
I don't know.


00:28:51.354 --> 00:28:52.605
Please!


00:28:52.688 --> 00:28:54.440
Gentlemen, you can enter.


00:28:54.523 --> 00:28:56.317
I don't know!


00:28:56.400 --> 00:28:58.611
<i>Copy that.</i>


00:29:05.117 --> 00:29:06.285
So it's in the walls.


00:29:07.662 --> 00:29:09.789
Let's get started.


00:29:12.375 --> 00:29:13.834
What does this bring to mind?


00:29:13.918 --> 00:29:15.378
Wagner.


00:29:15.461 --> 00:29:17.338
- Duvall.
- <i>Apocalypse Now.</i>


00:29:19.882 --> 00:29:22.218
I love the smell
of napalm in the morning.


00:29:37.441 --> 00:29:38.442
Nice view.


00:29:38.526 --> 00:29:40.361
Yeah, it was a big selling point.


00:29:40.444 --> 00:29:41.445
The sauce tastes really...


00:29:43.114 --> 00:29:44.448
The mint sauce.


00:29:44.532 --> 00:29:47.285
It's all right, it's all right.
We'll make do without. It's okay.


00:29:47.368 --> 00:29:48.744
That was Mommy's favorite.


00:29:48.828 --> 00:29:51.122
We can't have Easter dinner
without the mint sauce.


00:29:51.205 --> 00:29:52.832
That was Mommy's favorite.


00:29:52.915 --> 00:29:54.959
- We can't, we just can't.
- It's okay.


00:29:59.255 --> 00:30:01.173
Max, are you stoned?


00:30:02.174 --> 00:30:04.677
You get sloshed. I get stoned.


00:30:04.760 --> 00:30:06.178
What's the big deal?


00:30:07.471 --> 00:30:09.473
One's legal, one isn't. Go to your room.


00:30:11.976 --> 00:30:13.728
Wait, so...


00:30:13.811 --> 00:30:16.188
she spills mint sauce on me,


00:30:16.272 --> 00:30:18.899
and I'm the one who's sent to my room?


00:30:18.983 --> 00:30:21.277
When Mom was here,
she never would've dealt with this shit.


00:30:21.360 --> 00:30:24.155
Mom isn't here. I'm here, and you're
just gonna have to get used to that.


00:30:24.238 --> 00:30:26.449
Yeah. Of course Mom's not here.


00:30:26.532 --> 00:30:30.745
- Thanks to you.
- Max, go to your room now.


00:30:32.371 --> 00:30:34.790
Why couldn't you have been
the one who died?


00:30:39.003 --> 00:30:40.504
Fuck this shit.


00:30:44.383 --> 00:30:46.177
I'm sorry you had to witness that.


00:30:47.386 --> 00:30:49.555
I've seen worse.


00:30:52.683 --> 00:30:55.186
Lily, the Hersches are still here,


00:30:55.269 --> 00:30:57.772
and I bet they have loads
of spare mint sauce.


00:30:58.773 --> 00:31:00.191
What do you say, huh?


00:31:01.484 --> 00:31:03.652
But it won't have pine nuts.


00:31:03.736 --> 00:31:05.821
I bet you I can find those too.


00:31:09.617 --> 00:31:11.744
Hey, Ali, can you just wait a moment?


00:31:11.827 --> 00:31:13.746
- Sure.
- Sweetheart,


00:31:13.829 --> 00:31:16.374
why don't you get a sponge
and a towel from the kitchen?


00:31:16.457 --> 00:31:17.833
I'll help you clean up.


00:31:23.297 --> 00:31:24.465
Damn it!


00:31:25.508 --> 00:31:26.634
It's empty.


00:31:29.887 --> 00:31:31.055
No!


00:31:31.138 --> 00:31:32.848
Where are they?


00:31:32.932 --> 00:31:35.393
We don't know what you're looking for.


00:31:35.476 --> 00:31:39.397
Please, we've lived in this apartment
for seven years,


00:31:39.480 --> 00:31:42.400
and if there was something here,
I would know about it.


00:31:42.483 --> 00:31:45.319
You've been living here for seven years?


00:31:45.403 --> 00:31:50.116
My records indicate that you lived
at The Carrington for close to 30.


00:31:50.199 --> 00:31:52.743
We used to live upstairs.


00:31:52.827 --> 00:31:56.247
When Bernard had his stroke,
we wanted something on the ground floor,


00:31:56.330 --> 00:31:58.040
so we moved down here.


00:31:59.041 --> 00:32:01.001
There you have it.


00:32:01.085 --> 00:32:04.797
And which apartment
did you used to live in?


00:32:06.090 --> 00:32:08.342
- 10C.
- 10C.


00:32:09.343 --> 00:32:12.221
Thank you, Mrs. Hersch,
for your cooperation.


00:32:12.304 --> 00:32:14.056
10C is occupied.


00:32:14.140 --> 00:32:17.601
- Occupied?
- They delayed their move until Monday.


00:32:17.685 --> 00:32:19.437
He's a professor with two kids.


00:32:19.520 --> 00:32:23.190
You informed me the building would be
empty except for the Hersches.


00:32:23.274 --> 00:32:24.900
It's ten floors up.


00:32:24.984 --> 00:32:26.861
- I didn't think that...
- That's right.


00:32:26.944 --> 00:32:31.073
You didn't think. Well, do so now.


00:32:31.157 --> 00:32:33.033
Figure out what to do with them.


00:32:37.371 --> 00:32:39.206
- Let's go.
- Pack it up.


00:32:40.249 --> 00:32:41.459
I got these.


00:32:46.630 --> 00:32:52.344
Even that hoodlum sees you
for the vain brute you are.


00:32:56.724 --> 00:32:58.184
So now you talk?


00:33:02.563 --> 00:33:05.566
I can't tell you what it means
to the kids for you to be here.


00:33:06.984 --> 00:33:10.321
They have a unique way
of showing it, don't they?


00:33:10.404 --> 00:33:12.656
Well, you should see them on a bad day.


00:33:17.786 --> 00:33:19.246
I'm sorry, Ali.


00:33:21.749 --> 00:33:25.669
I mean, I feel blessed with my kids
and the time I had with Kate.


00:33:27.379 --> 00:33:29.173
But your sister wasn't the easiest person.


00:33:29.256 --> 00:33:30.841
Yeah, you married her.


00:33:32.176 --> 00:33:33.427
Yeah, you're right.


00:33:35.012 --> 00:33:37.598
We went through a rough patch.
I turned to you. I was wrong to do so.


00:33:37.681 --> 00:33:39.558
- Please, can we not...
- No, I thought about this for years.


00:33:39.642 --> 00:33:40.726
Just hear me out.


00:33:44.230 --> 00:33:46.065
You saw me as the man I wanted to be.


00:33:46.148 --> 00:33:49.568
You made me feel...
<i>You</i> made me feel.


00:33:49.652 --> 00:33:52.238
And then I wake up one morning, and you've
gone. What am I supposed to think?


00:33:52.321 --> 00:33:53.989
I went off to serve my country.


00:33:54.073 --> 00:33:57.576
Oh, come on. That's an absurd
rationalization if ever I've heard one.


00:33:59.245 --> 00:34:01.997
I understand. You're in pain.


00:34:02.081 --> 00:34:05.668
But I was never gonna be the person
to ruin my sister's marriage.


00:34:05.751 --> 00:34:07.086
How do you think I felt?


00:34:07.169 --> 00:34:10.089
What, so you sign up
as a lifer in the Marines?


00:34:10.172 --> 00:34:12.716
It's almost a cliche.


00:34:13.717 --> 00:34:15.219
What do you want from me?


00:34:17.555 --> 00:34:19.139
Ali, I never meant to hurt you.


00:34:20.558 --> 00:34:23.143
To be honest, I don't really care anymore.


00:34:26.355 --> 00:34:27.648
But I do.


00:34:30.859 --> 00:34:34.071
I am going to get Lily
some mint sauce now.


00:34:53.007 --> 00:34:54.425
Mrs. Hersch?


00:34:54.508 --> 00:34:56.302
Mrs. Hersch?


00:35:00.681 --> 00:35:01.932
Oh, my God.


00:35:04.727 --> 00:35:05.936
Oh, my God.


00:35:14.069 --> 00:35:15.195
Borz.


00:35:16.196 --> 00:35:17.615
<i>Borz, are you there?</i>


00:35:19.408 --> 00:35:20.576
<i>Hello?</i>


00:35:20.659 --> 00:35:22.244
Borz, call the police.
The Hersches are dead.


00:35:22.328 --> 00:35:23.454
<i>I cannot hear you.</i>


00:35:23.537 --> 00:35:25.080
Can you please come to the lobby?


00:35:26.081 --> 00:35:27.124
<i>Hello?</i>


00:35:27.207 --> 00:35:28.208
Shit.


00:35:32.546 --> 00:35:34.089
Ali?


00:35:34.173 --> 00:35:36.008
Ali, did you get it?


00:35:36.091 --> 00:35:37.593
Hello, young lady.


00:35:40.137 --> 00:35:41.430
- Daddy.
- Hey, what's going on?


00:35:43.223 --> 00:35:44.308
Hey, who are you?


00:35:44.391 --> 00:35:47.561
Good evening.
My name is Victor Dubois.


00:35:47.645 --> 00:35:50.272
Sorry for the unannounced arrival.


00:35:51.815 --> 00:35:56.236
I promise our visit will be as brief
as humanly possible.


00:35:56.320 --> 00:35:58.781
- Who are they?
- It's okay, sweetie.


00:35:58.864 --> 00:36:01.075
We do what they say
and everything will be fine.


00:36:01.158 --> 00:36:03.619
- What if it isn't fine?
- Shh...


00:36:05.746 --> 00:36:07.706
Borz, what's going on?
I just tried to call you.


00:36:07.790 --> 00:36:10.501
The intercom is not working.
The phones are down. I don't know.


00:36:10.584 --> 00:36:12.294
The Hersches are dead.


00:36:12.378 --> 00:36:13.921
- What?
- Call the police.


00:36:31.814 --> 00:36:32.815
Fuck.


00:36:44.743 --> 00:36:47.246
Come on, come on. Come on.


00:36:49.623 --> 00:36:52.334
- This is a big place.
- Yeah, this may take a while.


00:36:52.418 --> 00:36:54.545
- Get the tools out.
- I got these.


00:36:54.628 --> 00:36:55.713
Let's go. Let's get moving.


00:36:55.796 --> 00:36:57.715
No need to hide your phone.


00:36:57.798 --> 00:36:59.675
You'll find there is no service.


00:37:01.385 --> 00:37:03.387
Quite the collection you have here.


00:37:04.513 --> 00:37:07.057
A fan of European history, are you?


00:37:08.058 --> 00:37:09.351
I teach it at Columbia.


00:37:09.435 --> 00:37:12.062
Oh. A professor.


00:37:13.814 --> 00:37:14.898
Goya.


00:37:14.982 --> 00:37:17.067
One of <i>Los Caprichos.</i>


00:37:17.151 --> 00:37:19.361
Very good taste, Mr. Stanton.


00:37:19.445 --> 00:37:20.946
You know your art.


00:37:21.029 --> 00:37:24.867
I admire how an artist
can dip his brush into his soul


00:37:24.950 --> 00:37:27.619
and capture his times in paintings.


00:37:27.703 --> 00:37:31.498
It appears Goya captured
our times as well.


00:37:31.582 --> 00:37:35.461
The picture's called <i>The Sleep of Reason
Produces Monsters.</i>


00:37:36.545 --> 00:37:37.504
Hi, guys.


00:37:39.673 --> 00:37:40.674
- Hi, Jon.
- Borz.


00:37:40.758 --> 00:37:43.302
- What is this about?
- It'll be fine.


00:37:43.385 --> 00:37:46.555
Pee-Wee, there's a girl trapped
in the elevator on the eighth floor.


00:37:46.638 --> 00:37:47.931
He's talking about Ali.


00:37:48.015 --> 00:37:49.683
Can you go take care of it?


00:37:52.060 --> 00:37:53.979
Everything okay?


00:37:54.062 --> 00:37:55.939
- Everything's super.
- Ah.


00:37:56.023 --> 00:37:58.108
Hi, Lily. Happy Easter.


00:37:59.109 --> 00:38:00.444
Hi, Borz.


00:38:11.371 --> 00:38:12.915
Where's Max?


00:38:12.998 --> 00:38:15.501
He's with his aunt for Easter
in the Hamptons.


00:38:18.337 --> 00:38:19.421
Max?


00:38:20.798 --> 00:38:25.177
I find it interesting that you set up
a place for him here at your table.


00:38:26.178 --> 00:38:27.304
Go find him.


00:38:54.998 --> 00:38:57.209
Hey, buddy.


00:39:21.149 --> 00:39:24.069
- We can start the work, Martinez.
- Copy.


00:39:24.152 --> 00:39:27.531
Okay, let's start here, here and here.


00:39:27.614 --> 00:39:30.492
- Hey, what are you doing?
- Shut up! Sit down.


00:40:15.245 --> 00:40:16.622
Hey, sweet thing.


00:40:44.900 --> 00:40:47.194
I smell you.


00:40:48.195 --> 00:40:49.488
Oh, yeah.


00:41:07.255 --> 00:41:09.216
Who are you and what do you want?


00:41:26.733 --> 00:41:28.151
Where are you?


00:41:51.883 --> 00:41:53.885
You're a twisted bitch, ain't you?


00:41:55.095 --> 00:41:56.513
You're not a Virgo, are you?


00:41:57.556 --> 00:42:01.184
I dated one of those.
Always had to choose the movies.


00:42:01.268 --> 00:42:02.686
It was a disaster.


00:42:03.979 --> 00:42:05.230
I'm a Gemini.


00:42:06.690 --> 00:42:07.858
What are you?


00:42:24.708 --> 00:42:27.294
I'm a Scorpio. It would never work.


00:42:31.423 --> 00:42:32.799
Max?


00:42:32.883 --> 00:42:34.217
<i>Pee-Wee?</i>


00:42:34.384 --> 00:42:35.427
Pee-Wee?


00:42:36.845 --> 00:42:37.971
Please, just stop.


00:42:38.055 --> 00:42:39.723
Nothing in this wall.


00:42:39.806 --> 00:42:42.184
Tell me what you want. I'll give you
anything, just leave us alone.


00:42:42.267 --> 00:42:45.187
I appreciate your kind offer,
but in this instance,


00:42:45.270 --> 00:42:47.647
I don't believe
you can be of assistance.


00:42:47.731 --> 00:42:49.608
Pee-Wee, come in.


00:42:49.691 --> 00:42:51.818
- What's going on?
- Pee-Wee's not answering.


00:42:51.902 --> 00:42:53.236
Take Leo and check it out.


00:42:53.320 --> 00:42:56.948
Perhaps it is just a problem
with Pee-Wee's radio.


00:42:57.032 --> 00:42:58.909
As you taught me,
it's better to cover every scenario.


00:43:00.243 --> 00:43:03.121
And when you're down in the lobby, turn
the elevators on so we can use them.


00:43:03.205 --> 00:43:04.873
And what scenario am I missing?


00:43:08.210 --> 00:43:10.378
There's a doorman in the building.


00:43:12.506 --> 00:43:13.673
It's just a girl.


00:43:14.758 --> 00:43:16.676
It's nothing to worry about.


00:43:16.760 --> 00:43:17.928
<i>Max, what happened?</i>


00:43:19.596 --> 00:43:22.724
Sweetie, I am sorry that you had
to see that, but I need you to focus.


00:43:22.808 --> 00:43:24.392
Tell me everything that you know.


00:43:25.602 --> 00:43:26.728
Max.


00:43:29.648 --> 00:43:30.774
You killed him.


00:43:32.859 --> 00:43:34.653
Listen, the only thing
that matters right now


00:43:34.736 --> 00:43:37.823
is where he came from
and how we can stop them.


00:43:37.906 --> 00:43:40.575
A bunch of guys with guns
broke into our apartment.


00:43:40.659 --> 00:43:42.536
They've got my dad and sister.


00:43:43.745 --> 00:43:45.080
Okay. How many guys?


00:43:45.163 --> 00:43:47.457
I don't know. Four, maybe five.


00:43:48.458 --> 00:43:49.626
Borz is with them.


00:43:49.709 --> 00:43:51.837
- I figured.
- And some French dude.


00:43:51.920 --> 00:43:54.089
I think he might be their leader.


00:43:56.091 --> 00:43:57.551
This is so twisted.


00:43:59.678 --> 00:44:01.429
Focus, Max.


00:44:01.513 --> 00:44:04.850
You know your way around this building.
I don't. I need you.


00:44:04.933 --> 00:44:07.060
Your family needs you.


00:44:08.311 --> 00:44:10.313
What would they want
in your apartment anyway?


00:44:10.397 --> 00:44:14.317
I'm telling you, man,
this shit is messed up.


00:44:14.401 --> 00:44:16.778
Did you see Borz
cutting that old man's leg?


00:44:17.779 --> 00:44:20.824
He was enjoying that shit. You saw it.


00:44:22.868 --> 00:44:24.870
I don't know, man.


00:44:24.953 --> 00:44:26.788
I don't know if this job is worth it.


00:44:27.789 --> 00:44:31.084
Hey, how much you getting paid anyway?
Twenty-five?


00:44:32.460 --> 00:44:33.628
What, thirty?


00:44:46.808 --> 00:44:47.809
<i>Borz, come in.</i>


00:44:48.810 --> 00:44:49.853
Yeah, copy.


00:44:50.854 --> 00:44:53.315
<i>We found Pee-Wee. He's dead.</i>


00:44:56.067 --> 00:44:58.653
This is how you have things under control?


00:45:02.490 --> 00:45:04.743
- Find her and kill her.
- <i>Copy.</i>


00:45:08.538 --> 00:45:10.457
- Go, go, go.
- What was that?


00:45:10.540 --> 00:45:11.875
Go, go.


00:45:14.794 --> 00:45:16.129
I see 'em! Get 'em!


00:45:27.974 --> 00:45:29.142
Max?


00:45:30.685 --> 00:45:33.438
There's a room behind
one of these walls.


00:45:33.521 --> 00:45:36.441
Pat told me.
He called it a hidden sanctuary.


00:45:49.788 --> 00:45:51.206
I got it. I got it.


00:46:08.223 --> 00:46:10.558
Not exactly the sanctuary
I was expecting.


00:46:13.812 --> 00:46:16.064
Borz? Borz, come in.


00:46:16.147 --> 00:46:17.774
- <i>Copy.</i>
- I got 'em.


00:46:20.151 --> 00:46:21.152
We lost them.


00:46:21.236 --> 00:46:24.114
You lost them? Who's "them"?


00:46:24.197 --> 00:46:26.283
- <i>She's got a kid with her.</i>
- It's Max.


00:46:27.284 --> 00:46:28.493
<i>She's armed.</i>


00:46:32.205 --> 00:46:33.331
Keep looking.


00:46:38.420 --> 00:46:41.339
- You know Morse?
- I was a Scout once.


00:46:45.343 --> 00:46:48.513
- So what is this place?
- It's a speakeasy.


00:46:48.596 --> 00:46:51.599
During Prohibition, residents
would meet here in secret to get wasted.


00:46:53.143 --> 00:46:55.145
Not on my watch. Come on.
What are you doing?


00:46:55.228 --> 00:46:58.023
- You're not my mom.
- Exactly. Sit down.


00:46:58.106 --> 00:47:00.483
How'd she get into the building?


00:47:01.609 --> 00:47:03.737
- I let her in.
- Really?


00:47:03.820 --> 00:47:05.989
Yeah, she was having dinner here
with the Stantons, and [...


00:47:06.072 --> 00:47:07.532
Thought she was on the tenth floor?


00:47:07.615 --> 00:47:09.701
- Yeah.
- You idiot.


00:47:13.663 --> 00:47:16.333
So, she was having dinner here?


00:47:16.416 --> 00:47:19.961
What light can you shed
on our mysterious lady?


00:47:22.297 --> 00:47:24.716
Nothing. I just met her.


00:47:25.884 --> 00:47:28.887
You invited a stranger
to share Easter dinner?


00:47:29.888 --> 00:47:31.473
She must be very beautiful.


00:47:32.724 --> 00:47:35.101
She helped my children
save Jasper, our cat.


00:47:35.185 --> 00:47:37.187
She's new here.
It was the least we could do.


00:47:38.229 --> 00:47:40.065
Who is this doorwoman?


00:47:42.108 --> 00:47:43.109
You have a name?


00:47:44.110 --> 00:47:45.111
Ali.


00:47:45.195 --> 00:47:46.404
Ali what?


00:47:47.489 --> 00:47:49.949
Her full name...
Something Polish.


00:47:50.950 --> 00:47:52.118
Gorski.


00:47:57.332 --> 00:47:59.584
- Oh.
- What?


00:48:01.669 --> 00:48:05.131
"Gunnery Sergeant Alexandra Gorski
of the Marine Security Guard brigade


00:48:05.215 --> 00:48:11.262
received a Silver Star for her actions
on October 15, 2019


00:48:11.346 --> 00:48:14.849
during a terrorist ambush
on the ambassador's convoy


00:48:14.933 --> 00:48:17.227
in Bucharest, Romania.


00:48:17.310 --> 00:48:19.646
Gorski is only the third female soldier


00:48:19.729 --> 00:48:24.776
to receive the award for exceptional valor
since World War ll."


00:48:24.859 --> 00:48:28.696
What's a decorated soldier
doing here as a doorman?


00:48:29.823 --> 00:48:31.449
Why didn't you talk to my mom?


00:48:32.784 --> 00:48:34.828
That's a long story.


00:48:36.454 --> 00:48:39.416
What about my dad?
You guys clearly knew each other.


00:48:40.542 --> 00:48:41.835
He was kind of an ass.


00:48:42.836 --> 00:48:44.421
Yeah, still is.


00:48:44.504 --> 00:48:47.090
I didn't mean that. He is a good man.


00:48:47.173 --> 00:48:48.883
My dad's a pussy.


00:48:48.967 --> 00:48:50.218
No, he's not.


00:48:51.928 --> 00:48:53.721
You don't know anything about him.


00:48:53.805 --> 00:48:57.100
A dad raising two kids
on his own is not a coward.


00:48:59.310 --> 00:49:01.729
My mom and dad were driving back
from the theater.


00:49:03.773 --> 00:49:04.899
I was on the phone with my mom


00:49:04.983 --> 00:49:07.360
when the car slid off the road
into the lake.


00:49:08.528 --> 00:49:10.280
My mom was trapped inside.


00:49:13.950 --> 00:49:15.326
Dad made it out.


00:49:16.327 --> 00:49:17.328
She didn't.


00:49:19.622 --> 00:49:21.749
I'm sure that he tried
everything that he could.


00:49:21.833 --> 00:49:25.879
I was on the phone with her for a full
minute as the car filled with water.


00:49:25.962 --> 00:49:27.547
What was he doing all that time?


00:49:29.632 --> 00:49:31.050
He should've done more.


00:49:32.635 --> 00:49:35.263
- Don't you think he...
- He didn't fucking try hard enough!


00:49:38.558 --> 00:49:39.726
Did you hear that?


00:49:42.937 --> 00:49:44.022
Hey.


00:49:47.525 --> 00:49:49.402
Don't be ashamed.


00:49:49.486 --> 00:49:51.738
I've seen plenty of tough guys cry.


00:49:54.699 --> 00:49:56.367
I'm not my father.


00:49:58.495 --> 00:49:59.871
Max, what the hell?


00:50:05.251 --> 00:50:07.003
Christ. Give me that!


00:50:07.086 --> 00:50:08.963
Are you out of your goddamn mind?


00:50:11.508 --> 00:50:12.592
Let's go.


00:50:13.760 --> 00:50:16.387
Please tell me there's
another way out of this room.


00:50:17.597 --> 00:50:18.723
Check this out.


00:50:21.726 --> 00:50:22.810
What is it?


00:50:22.894 --> 00:50:25.063
This is how they got the liquor up here
without anybody noticing.


00:50:25.146 --> 00:50:26.272
Come on. It's our way out of here.


00:50:28.024 --> 00:50:30.777
Okay. Okay.


00:50:30.860 --> 00:50:32.987
Well, there are six more rooms.


00:50:33.071 --> 00:50:36.366
If we have to tear down every wall,
we're gonna be here until Christmas.


00:50:40.161 --> 00:50:42.080
So what now, Mr. Dubois?


00:50:46.751 --> 00:50:48.002
They're here.


00:50:51.381 --> 00:50:52.590
They have to be.


00:50:59.013 --> 00:51:01.224
Okay, slowly. Slowly.


00:51:26.374 --> 00:51:27.667
Watch out, man, I got this.


00:51:27.750 --> 00:51:28.585
Go!


00:51:32.046 --> 00:51:37.343
You have amassed quite a library
over the years, Mr. Stanton.


00:51:38.886 --> 00:51:44.267
The books I've collected
have been an important part of my work.


00:51:44.350 --> 00:51:48.021
With a distinct bent
towards British history.


00:51:51.357 --> 00:51:53.526
Well, you can take the boy out of England,


00:51:53.610 --> 00:51:56.446
but you can't take England out of the boy.


00:51:59.532 --> 00:52:01.743
You must have spent a small fortune


00:52:01.826 --> 00:52:05.705
to build shelves capable
of storing your collection.


00:52:06.706 --> 00:52:08.625
The former tenant built the library.


00:52:08.708 --> 00:52:11.127
It was one of the main reasons
why we bought this place.


00:52:15.506 --> 00:52:16.799
What the hell are you doing?


00:52:16.883 --> 00:52:19.719
I never knew Dreischler
to be a big reader.


00:52:19.802 --> 00:52:22.847
- Dreischler?
- Your Mr. Hersch.


00:52:38.696 --> 00:52:40.865
Borz, get the tools!


00:52:46.663 --> 00:52:49.999
A customized Mosler from the early '80s,
four-wheel combination lock.


00:52:51.626 --> 00:52:52.960
This isn't gonna be easy.


00:52:53.044 --> 00:52:54.379
How long?


00:52:54.462 --> 00:52:58.007
Good safecracker would get you
inside within five hours.


00:52:59.008 --> 00:53:01.594
- I'll do it in two.
- Do it in one.


00:53:12.355 --> 00:53:16.192
No, no, no. We need the water
to cool the drill bit, man. Yeah.


00:53:16.275 --> 00:53:18.277
Grab the hose
and hook it up in the kitchen.


00:53:18.361 --> 00:53:21.948
You're telling me what to do now?
Who put you in charge?


00:53:22.031 --> 00:53:23.991
Get him what he needs.


00:53:28.746 --> 00:53:31.874
I opened a vintage bottle of wine
for the holidays.


00:53:33.126 --> 00:53:34.877
Would you care to join me for a glass?


00:53:34.961 --> 00:53:36.754
That would be splendid.


00:53:45.179 --> 00:53:46.264
Would you like some?


00:53:49.016 --> 00:53:50.727
Huh. I'll take that as a no.


00:54:12.457 --> 00:54:14.375
Here we are, Mr. Dubois. Enjoy.


00:54:18.045 --> 00:54:20.715
Mm. That's an old Italian.


00:54:21.716 --> 00:54:23.384
I prefer Bordeaux.


00:54:24.969 --> 00:54:27.305
- Hmm.
- It was a gift.


00:54:27.388 --> 00:54:29.307
I'm not much of a connoisseur myself.


00:54:33.102 --> 00:54:35.271
Sweetheart, can you
hold this for a second?


00:55:12.183 --> 00:55:14.018
Not like your video games, is it?


00:55:27.865 --> 00:55:28.866
Turn around.


00:55:39.335 --> 00:55:42.547
I've been wondering
how long ago you met Mr. Hersch.


00:55:43.756 --> 00:55:45.508
Why do you ask?


00:55:45.591 --> 00:55:48.678
Oh, just habit. Too many years
in research libraries.


00:55:48.761 --> 00:55:51.055
My wife used to say I asked
too many questions.


00:55:52.098 --> 00:55:54.267
Over 30 years.


00:55:54.350 --> 00:55:55.643
Oh, interesting.


00:55:55.726 --> 00:55:57.436
A Frenchman and a German.


00:55:57.520 --> 00:55:59.522
Is the water running?


00:55:59.605 --> 00:56:00.815
What's it look like?


00:56:05.611 --> 00:56:07.864
Historically speaking,
you haven't always gotten along.


00:56:07.947 --> 00:56:10.616
We had common
business interests.


00:56:10.700 --> 00:56:11.701
Oh, Borz.


00:56:13.411 --> 00:56:15.580
Uh, where did you meet him?


00:56:17.164 --> 00:56:21.210
He doesn't strike me as intelligent enough
to move in your circles.


00:56:21.294 --> 00:56:23.421
Let me guess. Uh, prison?


00:56:24.839 --> 00:56:28.843
You've done a splendid job of deduction,
Mr. Stanton.


00:56:28.926 --> 00:56:30.887
Borz and I did meet in prison.


00:56:30.970 --> 00:56:33.306
I don't think you should give him
this kind of information.


00:56:34.307 --> 00:56:36.767
Down, Borz. It is okay.


00:56:38.603 --> 00:56:40.521
Borz, I need a hand.


00:56:41.731 --> 00:56:42.857
Coming.


00:56:46.569 --> 00:56:48.112
- Damn it.
- They locked us in.


00:56:53.743 --> 00:56:56.287
Phones are dead.


00:56:56.370 --> 00:56:58.331
Hey, do you know where
the main panel is?


00:56:58.414 --> 00:57:00.082
Yeah, control room. This way.


00:57:06.088 --> 00:57:09.675
Okay, well, you can forget about getting
the phone lines to work again.


00:57:10.801 --> 00:57:12.219
What about the fire alarm?


00:57:12.303 --> 00:57:13.304
That's a good idea.


00:57:14.347 --> 00:57:15.514
Okay.


00:57:20.144 --> 00:57:21.145
Okay.


00:57:31.322 --> 00:57:33.324
Boom. One down!


00:57:33.407 --> 00:57:37.036
May I ask...
what you're looking for?


00:57:37.119 --> 00:57:39.205
Perhaps I can help.


00:57:39.288 --> 00:57:41.874
What have you learned is my passion?


00:57:41.958 --> 00:57:43.668
Well, your love for art.


00:57:43.751 --> 00:57:47.129
And how long ago did I meet Mr. Hersch?


00:57:47.213 --> 00:57:49.507
Over 30 years.


00:57:49.590 --> 00:57:51.801
In East Germany, to be precise.


00:57:51.884 --> 00:57:54.428
And you, the learned scholar,


00:57:54.512 --> 00:57:58.557
can you tell me what were the most
prominent events there at that time?


00:57:58.641 --> 00:58:02.228
The last days of
the German Democratic Republic,


00:58:02.311 --> 00:58:04.105
the fall of East Berlin,
the Wall coming down.


00:58:04.188 --> 00:58:05.773
Bravo.


00:58:05.856 --> 00:58:10.778
Dreischler... I mean, your Mr. Hersch
was in charge of the KoKo program,


00:58:10.861 --> 00:58:16.659
requisitioning the most valuable assets
of East German citizens.


00:58:16.742 --> 00:58:18.786
I see.


00:58:18.869 --> 00:58:23.207
And you were brought in to fence them off,
to finance a bankrupt government.


00:58:23.290 --> 00:58:28.087
I was trying to save those works
so the rest of the world could enjoy them.


00:58:28.170 --> 00:58:29.922
If it weren't for my efforts,


00:58:30.006 --> 00:58:34.176
they could have been lost
forever behind an Iron Curtain.


00:58:36.262 --> 00:58:37.638
Gosh, you delude yourself.


00:58:37.722 --> 00:58:39.849
I came to take what is mine, Professor!


00:58:39.932 --> 00:58:43.144
I paid for it
with the best years of my life.


00:58:45.896 --> 00:58:47.648
Hey! What are you doing?


00:58:47.732 --> 00:58:48.733
Give me that.


00:58:50.985 --> 00:58:52.528
What?


00:58:52.611 --> 00:58:53.821
So what do we do now?


00:58:55.448 --> 00:58:56.574
Delete it.


00:58:56.657 --> 00:58:58.868
- You come here.
- No, don't touch my daughter!


00:58:58.951 --> 00:59:00.036
Daddy!


00:59:01.454 --> 00:59:02.830
Yeah, come on. Come on.


00:59:02.913 --> 00:59:04.498
- Stop!
- Come on. Come on.


00:59:06.917 --> 00:59:09.336
Remember, we are civilized.


00:59:10.337 --> 00:59:11.630
You talk too much.


00:59:12.923 --> 00:59:14.133
Delete it!


00:59:17.094 --> 00:59:19.972
Okay. All right, pull that.


00:59:26.937 --> 00:59:27.772
Got it. Let's go.


00:59:33.194 --> 00:59:34.403
What is that?


00:59:34.487 --> 00:59:35.654
It's the fire alarm.


00:59:35.738 --> 00:59:38.157
I know it's the fire alarm, you idiot.


00:59:38.240 --> 00:59:41.869
I specifically instructed you
to disable it.


00:59:43.913 --> 00:59:45.122
I'll handle it.


00:59:57.343 --> 00:59:58.177
Ali?


01:00:04.850 --> 01:00:06.560
Can you come in here for a second?


01:00:12.441 --> 01:00:14.735
Drop the guns. Slowly.


01:00:19.490 --> 01:00:20.699
Step away from the door.


01:00:22.118 --> 01:00:23.327
Behind the wall.


01:00:24.912 --> 01:00:28.290
One word from you, and I'll shoot the kid.
Understood?


01:00:30.709 --> 01:00:32.753
- Come on!
- I'm coming.


01:00:32.837 --> 01:00:33.921
Sorry.


01:00:36.841 --> 01:00:38.342
- What's going on here?
- Hey.


01:00:38.425 --> 01:00:40.886
Um... Just a false alarm.


01:00:40.970 --> 01:00:42.763
What do you mean it's a false alarm?


01:00:51.939 --> 01:00:55.192
Some of the contractors
might have crossed the wires.


01:00:55.276 --> 01:00:56.986
Something. I don't know.


01:00:57.069 --> 01:00:58.654
Why is the door locked?


01:00:58.737 --> 01:01:02.658
There's no one else here
because of the remodel,


01:01:02.741 --> 01:01:04.285
except for some construction guys.


01:01:04.368 --> 01:01:07.121
You can't lock the door.
It's illegal and it's dangerous.


01:01:07.204 --> 01:01:09.415
Yeah, but the entire building
is locked down.


01:01:09.498 --> 01:01:12.084
It's closed up, so we're using
the service doors.


01:01:12.168 --> 01:01:13.586
What did I miss?


01:01:13.669 --> 01:01:15.254
- Well...


01:01:15.337 --> 01:01:16.505
It's a false alarm.


01:01:16.589 --> 01:01:18.382
City regulations say we gotta check it.


01:01:18.465 --> 01:01:21.051
- Floor by floor.
- Ten floors? Go ahead.


01:01:21.135 --> 01:01:22.678
Come on, Captain.


01:01:22.761 --> 01:01:24.847
Easter dinner's getting cold
at the station.


01:01:24.930 --> 01:01:26.432
Hey, regulations is regulations.


01:01:26.515 --> 01:01:28.934
Come on, Chief.
Give your guys a break.


01:01:29.018 --> 01:01:31.896
We can bend the rules a little.
Clearly there's nothing wrong here.


01:01:31.979 --> 01:01:34.398
Absolutely not.
False alarm, a hundred percent.


01:01:35.399 --> 01:01:36.734
All right.


01:01:36.817 --> 01:01:39.945
You just keep your carpenters
away from my fire alarm system.


01:01:40.029 --> 01:01:42.281
Absolutely. Won't happen again, sir.


01:01:42.364 --> 01:01:43.616
Let's go.


01:01:43.699 --> 01:01:46.035
Hey, another false alarm
and you'll get fined.


01:01:46.118 --> 01:01:48.412
Thank you very much, sir.
I highly appreciate it.


01:01:48.495 --> 01:01:51.040
Okay, party's over.


01:01:51.123 --> 01:01:53.417
Thank you. Happy Easter!


01:01:57.129 --> 01:02:00.841
Nice try, Gorski.


01:02:06.305 --> 01:02:08.182
You aroused my curiosity, though.


01:02:08.265 --> 01:02:11.727
Why would a decorated officer
hole up here as a doorman?


01:02:11.810 --> 01:02:13.896
To meet interesting people like you.


01:02:15.606 --> 01:02:17.608
I had a friend...


01:02:17.691 --> 01:02:21.111
that came back after war,
and he was damaged.


01:02:21.195 --> 01:02:23.697
Are you damaged, soldier?


01:02:26.283 --> 01:02:27.910
Not as damaged as you.


01:02:33.290 --> 01:02:34.333
What about this...


01:02:41.215 --> 01:02:42.675
Get their guns!


01:02:46.095 --> 01:02:48.514
Take the gun.
Max, give me the rifle.


01:02:48.597 --> 01:02:49.723
Find a way out. You go that way.


01:02:50.891 --> 01:02:52.643
Come on. Get her!


01:02:57.773 --> 01:02:59.441
There she is! Hey!


01:05:34.263 --> 01:05:35.264
Find the kid.


01:05:37.182 --> 01:05:38.642
I'm gonna kill that bitch.


01:06:49.046 --> 01:06:53.008
<i>Yeah, the car runs
on an app, and the app needs a signal.</i>


01:06:54.301 --> 01:06:55.802
- <i>Oh, my God.</i>
- <i>Right.</i>


01:06:55.886 --> 01:06:57.721
<i>So halfway up a mountain,
no one for miles...</i>


01:06:57.804 --> 01:06:59.515
Officer.


01:06:59.598 --> 01:07:02.267
What is it? You okay?


01:07:02.351 --> 01:07:04.978
There are terrorists in The Carrington.
You've got to call police, SWAT, everyone.


01:07:05.062 --> 01:07:07.189
Hold on, hold on.
Terrorists in The Carrington?


01:07:07.272 --> 01:07:08.982
My dad and sister,
they've been kidnapped.


01:07:09.066 --> 01:07:11.109
Kidnapped?


01:07:11.193 --> 01:07:15.489
This is 105 Charlie. I got a 10-10 here
at 85th and Central Park West.


01:07:15.572 --> 01:07:17.241
Yeah, there's a kid that claims


01:07:17.324 --> 01:07:19.243
The Carrington's been
taken over by terrorists.


01:07:19.326 --> 01:07:21.620
- What's your name?
- Max Stanton.


01:07:21.703 --> 01:07:23.455
His name is Max Stanton.


01:07:24.581 --> 01:07:26.083
They want to speak to you.


01:07:28.293 --> 01:07:30.254
- Hello?
- <i>Hello, Max.</i>


01:07:30.337 --> 01:07:31.838
<i>We miss you up here.</i>


01:07:33.257 --> 01:07:34.591
Let's go, kid.


01:07:34.675 --> 01:07:37.052
- Stay back.
- Whoa! Hold on, easy.


01:07:38.345 --> 01:07:39.888
How about you give me that gun, kid?


01:07:39.972 --> 01:07:41.723
- I'll shoot you, you cocksucker.
- Yeah?


01:07:41.807 --> 01:07:44.101
You gonna spray my brains
all over the car?


01:07:53.485 --> 01:07:54.528
Good boy.


01:08:03.287 --> 01:08:05.581
How's it going? Huh?


01:08:19.344 --> 01:08:20.762
<i>Ms. Gorski.</i>


01:08:27.477 --> 01:08:28.812
<i>Ms. Gorski?</i>


01:08:34.860 --> 01:08:37.529
Ms. Gorski, can you hear me?


01:08:37.613 --> 01:08:39.698
<i>Whoever you are
and whatever you're up to,</i>


01:08:39.781 --> 01:08:41.366
you should walk away now.


01:08:41.450 --> 01:08:43.952
<i>Someone's bringing in
the police to bring you down.</i>


01:08:44.036 --> 01:08:46.538
And if they don't stop you, I will.


01:08:46.622 --> 01:08:50.083
Things don't always work out
as we might wish.


01:08:50.167 --> 01:08:51.460
You, of all people,


01:08:51.543 --> 01:08:55.255
<i>should understand that, Sergeant Gorski.</i>


01:08:55.339 --> 01:08:59.635
By the way, I have someone here
who wants to say hello.


01:09:02.763 --> 01:09:04.222
<i>I'm sorry, Ali.</i>


01:09:08.060 --> 01:09:10.562
The Internet is a marvelous invention.


01:09:11.605 --> 01:09:13.565
<i>I was fascinated to read</i>


01:09:13.649 --> 01:09:17.486
<i>about what happened while you were
in the service at the embassy.</i>


01:09:17.569 --> 01:09:21.490
Unless you want more innocent
blood on your hands,


01:09:21.573 --> 01:09:26.703
be here in 15 minutes, unarmed,
and surrender. It's over.


01:09:42.386 --> 01:09:45.305
Come on, come on.
Now, right? Like, that's nothing.


01:09:50.936 --> 01:09:52.646
Two! Whoo!


01:09:58.902 --> 01:09:59.903
<i>Ali?</i>


01:10:04.241 --> 01:10:07.452
<i>Nothing's going to happen to you, okay?
Nothing's going to happen to you.</i>


01:12:07.030 --> 01:12:08.156
Why did you stop?


01:12:09.366 --> 01:12:12.786
There's no water and we need water.


01:12:12.869 --> 01:12:14.371
Check the faucet.


01:12:19.751 --> 01:12:20.877
Nothing.


01:12:22.128 --> 01:12:23.171
Leo!


01:12:23.255 --> 01:12:25.173
- Yeah?
- Can you check the bathroom?


01:12:40.355 --> 01:12:43.775
- No water in the bathroom.
- Is that bitch in the basement?


01:12:44.818 --> 01:12:47.153
We have no time for this. Keep drilling.


01:12:47.237 --> 01:12:48.947
Uh, no. No, no, no.


01:12:49.030 --> 01:12:52.951
You see, the drill bit, it'll break.
We need the water to keep it cool.


01:12:53.034 --> 01:12:55.745
Keep drilling! That's an order.


01:12:56.955 --> 01:12:58.957
Okay. Okay.


01:13:12.971 --> 01:13:17.017
I've got... We need water.


01:13:17.100 --> 01:13:18.184
<i>Merde.</i>


01:13:19.185 --> 01:13:21.521
He created this mess, you fix it.


01:13:21.605 --> 01:13:24.274
Go! Turn on the water.


01:13:25.275 --> 01:13:26.318
Yes, sir.


01:15:12.966 --> 01:15:14.384
<i>Leo, what's going on?</i>


01:15:15.385 --> 01:15:16.678
What's taking so long?


01:15:19.222 --> 01:15:21.599
You know, we are so, so close.


01:15:21.683 --> 01:15:24.185
I mean, I'm on the last lock. Come on.


01:15:25.937 --> 01:15:27.147
<i>Leo?</i>


01:15:32.235 --> 01:15:33.862
<i>He's dead and you're next.</i>


01:15:39.284 --> 01:15:45.582
It seems your doorwoman friend is more
effective than you gave her credit.


01:15:45.665 --> 01:15:48.710
I hear your putdowns.
I don't hear any solutions.


01:15:53.173 --> 01:15:54.007
What?


01:15:55.008 --> 01:15:56.217
Try this one.


01:16:02.307 --> 01:16:05.602
For someone like me
who appreciates fine art,


01:16:05.685 --> 01:16:09.898
I can say your daughter
has real talent.


01:16:09.981 --> 01:16:14.778
There is a certain likeness
in her drawing to this photo.


01:16:17.322 --> 01:16:19.699
If you just met Sergeant Gorski,


01:16:19.783 --> 01:16:24.079
why there is a photo of you
together when you were younger?


01:16:26.873 --> 01:16:31.669
I noticed your daughter's signature
and her reference to "Aunt Ali."


01:16:31.753 --> 01:16:37.801
I assume you are related
to the war hero killing all my men.


01:16:40.845 --> 01:16:44.390
Aunt Ali is smarter and stronger
than all of you.


01:16:44.474 --> 01:16:45.892
Honey. Honey, come here.


01:16:46.935 --> 01:16:48.603
Did I say something wrong?


01:16:48.686 --> 01:16:50.897
- No.
- No.


01:16:50.980 --> 01:16:53.441
Quite to the contrary.
You said something right.


01:16:53.525 --> 01:16:54.526
Thank you.


01:16:56.861 --> 01:17:01.699
<i>It appears you have been
withholding important information from us.</i>


01:17:01.783 --> 01:17:07.247
<i>I understand this kind of publicity
can get you discharged from the military.</i>


01:17:07.330 --> 01:17:09.707
<i>Isn't that true, Aunt Ali?</i>


01:17:14.921 --> 01:17:17.757
- Let them go, or I will...
- <i>Listen to me.</i>


01:17:17.841 --> 01:17:20.718
For every ten minutes
that pass without water,


01:17:20.802 --> 01:17:23.680
a member of your family will lose a limb.


01:17:23.763 --> 01:17:25.849
Now, turn on the water!


01:17:28.935 --> 01:17:31.688
Wait! The main water valve
has been destroyed.


01:17:34.107 --> 01:17:35.441
But I have a plan.


01:17:47.036 --> 01:17:48.204
Aunt Ali!


01:17:48.288 --> 01:17:49.747
Welcome, Sergeant Gorski.


01:17:51.332 --> 01:17:52.792
I am Victor Dubois.


01:17:54.586 --> 01:17:56.921
I accept your total surrender.


01:18:01.426 --> 01:18:03.595
Now listen to me, Victor.


01:18:03.678 --> 01:18:07.015
Once I get the water,
you release my family, and if you don't...


01:18:08.016 --> 01:18:09.350
I will take you to hell.


01:18:11.853 --> 01:18:16.649
I'm impressed someone in your position
negotiates from an illusion of strength.


01:18:18.026 --> 01:18:20.278
We have already established our terms.


01:18:21.279 --> 01:18:22.697
Now, the water.


01:18:41.341 --> 01:18:42.842
Officer Olsen, get up here.


01:19:02.320 --> 01:19:03.613
Now we wait.


01:19:07.533 --> 01:19:08.826
- We're back!
- Good.


01:19:08.910 --> 01:19:10.161
We got water!


01:19:15.708 --> 01:19:17.126
I kept up my end of the bargain.


01:19:18.127 --> 01:19:19.295
<i>Now it's yours.</i>


01:19:35.645 --> 01:19:37.939
We're in!


01:19:38.022 --> 01:19:39.023
We are in.


01:19:40.024 --> 01:19:41.067
We...


01:19:42.151 --> 01:19:45.571
are... in. Okay.


01:19:52.912 --> 01:19:53.955
Careful.


01:20:09.762 --> 01:20:11.014
Yeah.


01:20:11.097 --> 01:20:12.598
- Very good.
- Remove the box.


01:20:12.682 --> 01:20:13.725
Yes, sir.


01:20:23.443 --> 01:20:25.028
Is that what you were after?


01:20:25.111 --> 01:20:26.571
Nothing is...


01:20:28.531 --> 01:20:31.284
as it appears, Mr. Stanton.


01:20:33.995 --> 01:20:35.580
It's a Caravaggio.


01:20:37.081 --> 01:20:38.750
<i>The Nativity with St. Francis.</i>


01:20:54.515 --> 01:20:55.600
Rembrandt.


01:20:56.642 --> 01:20:58.061
It's a bloody Rembrandt.


01:21:20.166 --> 01:21:21.584
Bring the tubes.


01:21:24.379 --> 01:21:26.964
Be careful. Roll them gently.


01:21:30.968 --> 01:21:32.762
Do you know how much
these paintings are worth?


01:21:32.845 --> 01:21:35.681
- How much?
- Borz, time is of the essence.


01:21:35.765 --> 01:21:39.644
I don't know, $60 to $80 million.


01:21:40.937 --> 01:21:43.314
These paintings are worth $80 million?


01:21:43.398 --> 01:21:45.316
No, no, no. Each one.


01:21:49.445 --> 01:21:52.448
You told me these paintings
were worth $5 million max...


01:21:52.532 --> 01:21:54.117
We have an agreement.


01:21:54.200 --> 01:21:57.620
Said fee for services rendered.
End of discussion.


01:22:02.750 --> 01:22:04.836
Lily! Lily, get down.


01:22:10.508 --> 01:22:12.009
We don't have time for this.


01:22:12.093 --> 01:22:14.679
I absolutely agree. Pull the trigger
and see what happens.


01:22:18.975 --> 01:22:23.354
Do either of you know
how to move fine art?


01:22:27.692 --> 01:22:28.860
Do you know?


01:22:31.070 --> 01:22:34.740
Twenty-five percent for the both of us,
50% for you.


01:22:38.286 --> 01:22:39.912
Or we can all go down here.


01:22:44.167 --> 01:22:47.170
You're really coming into your own,
you know that?


01:22:58.473 --> 01:23:01.142
- Let's go.
- Okay.


01:23:04.353 --> 01:23:06.397
- Get up. Get up!
- Okay.


01:23:06.481 --> 01:23:08.274
Nobody moves!


01:23:08.357 --> 01:23:10.359
- No, no, no. Max!
- Sit down!


01:23:10.443 --> 01:23:11.819
Sit the fuck down!


01:23:11.903 --> 01:23:13.237
Or I shoot the kid.


01:23:16.032 --> 01:23:17.241
Let him go.


01:23:18.659 --> 01:23:20.119
See, this is where we're different.


01:23:21.120 --> 01:23:22.038
Martinez.


01:23:22.121 --> 01:23:23.581
Yeah?


01:23:23.664 --> 01:23:25.208
Guess it's a fifty-fifty.


01:23:25.291 --> 01:23:26.792
What?


01:23:33.716 --> 01:23:34.759
- Dad!
- No!


01:23:34.842 --> 01:23:36.260
Daddy!


01:23:47.396 --> 01:23:49.106
You should've taken a day off.


01:23:52.068 --> 01:23:53.319
No!


01:23:53.402 --> 01:23:54.946
Quick, quick!


01:23:59.575 --> 01:24:01.827
Dad! Dad, are you all right?


01:24:01.911 --> 01:24:03.329
It's okay.


01:24:04.330 --> 01:24:05.873
I underestimated you.


01:24:05.957 --> 01:24:07.291
Yeah, and I, you.


01:24:07.375 --> 01:24:08.918
Your dad's gonna be fine,


01:24:09.001 --> 01:24:11.754
but right now, I need you to be
his water wings, okay?


01:24:11.837 --> 01:24:13.673
So grab this.
Right here, hold it down.


01:24:15.841 --> 01:24:17.343
- Daddy? Daddy.
- I'm okay.


01:24:17.426 --> 01:24:19.095
- Daddy, I...
- I'm all right. I'm okay.


01:24:19.178 --> 01:24:21.097
Max, are you okay?


01:24:21.180 --> 01:24:22.723
I'm fine.


01:24:24.767 --> 01:24:26.018
Go get 'em.


01:24:30.898 --> 01:24:32.066
I'm gonna be okay.


01:24:38.322 --> 01:24:39.782
Go! Go! Go!


01:24:46.414 --> 01:24:48.249
- Hold it.
- Oh, my God! Don't shoot.


01:24:48.332 --> 01:24:50.543
- Hold it right there.
- I'm a doorman. I'm just a doorman.


01:24:50.626 --> 01:24:53.129
A woman went crazy.
She took her family hostage upstairs.


01:24:53.212 --> 01:24:55.089
She's coming down the stairs
right now. She's got a gun!


01:24:55.172 --> 01:24:57.091
Alpha team, spread out.


01:24:57.174 --> 01:25:00.094
Move to the exit, sir.
Move. Move, move, move.


01:25:01.596 --> 01:25:02.638
Seal the street.


01:25:05.766 --> 01:25:06.934
The building's surrounded.


01:25:07.935 --> 01:25:09.312
Plan B.


01:25:18.821 --> 01:25:20.406
Drop your weapon!


01:25:20.489 --> 01:25:21.574
Wait, wait.


01:25:21.657 --> 01:25:23.868
My brother-in-law is wounded
on the tenth floor.


01:25:23.951 --> 01:25:25.786
- He needs a medic.
- Drop it now!


01:25:25.870 --> 01:25:28.414
Please, it's not me.
It's Borz, the doorman.


01:25:28.497 --> 01:25:33.502
Step away from the weapon
and stand up slowly.


01:25:56.400 --> 01:25:58.402
I'm happy, Borz. You've changed.


01:25:58.486 --> 01:25:59.737
<i>Merde.</i>


01:26:03.282 --> 01:26:04.408
Yes, I have.


01:26:06.911 --> 01:26:08.245
One hundred percent.


01:26:10.623 --> 01:26:11.957
Borz.


01:26:30.893 --> 01:26:31.769
Borz!


01:26:35.564 --> 01:26:37.817
You're persistent, Sergeant.
I'll give you that.


01:26:39.110 --> 01:26:40.986
We have enough kissing ass
to do around here.


01:26:41.070 --> 01:26:43.030
We don't have to do it to each other.


01:26:43.114 --> 01:26:44.198
Let's finish this.


01:27:50.639 --> 01:27:52.266
What are you doing?
No, no, no!


01:27:52.349 --> 01:27:53.726
No! No!


01:28:00.441 --> 01:28:01.734
Are you crazy?!


01:28:34.642 --> 01:28:36.143
I knew you were sick.


01:28:37.394 --> 01:28:39.897
I just didn't realize how sick you were.


01:28:42.149 --> 01:28:43.234
Well, now you know.


01:28:53.702 --> 01:28:54.703
Fuck.


01:29:48.883 --> 01:29:51.385
Right. Do we have everything?


01:29:52.511 --> 01:29:53.387
Good.


01:29:54.388 --> 01:29:55.431
Hey, you.


01:29:57.182 --> 01:29:59.226
I didn't think I'd see you again.


01:29:59.310 --> 01:30:01.312
Thought you'd get rid of me
that easily, huh?


01:30:02.313 --> 01:30:03.564
How is he?


01:30:06.483 --> 01:30:07.568
He's all right.


01:30:10.279 --> 01:30:12.364
I'm sorry, Ali. This is all my fault.


01:30:14.158 --> 01:30:15.409
I couldn't do it.


01:30:16.410 --> 01:30:17.411
Do what?


01:30:18.412 --> 01:30:20.164
Use the gun.


01:30:20.247 --> 01:30:22.249
I wasn't the man you wanted me to be.


01:30:23.250 --> 01:30:25.502
I really like the man you are.


01:30:26.587 --> 01:30:27.796
Come on.


01:30:27.880 --> 01:30:29.757
- Aunt Ali!
- Hi.


01:30:30.966 --> 01:30:32.509
- Hi.
- Hi.


01:30:32.593 --> 01:30:34.094
I got you something.


01:30:36.972 --> 01:30:38.057
The mint sauce.


01:30:38.140 --> 01:30:40.643
With pine nuts, of course.


01:30:40.726 --> 01:30:42.102
Where's the lamb?


01:30:42.186 --> 01:30:45.314
The lamb.
I knew I forgot something.


01:30:47.191 --> 01:30:48.525
How are you?


01:30:48.609 --> 01:30:50.653
Oh, I'll manage.


01:30:50.736 --> 01:30:53.864
In a couple of weeks,
I'll be back to my usual boring self.


01:30:55.407 --> 01:30:57.660
- Sir, we should go.
- All right. Jump in.


01:30:58.661 --> 01:31:00.162
Bye, Aunt Ali.


01:31:03.290 --> 01:31:04.833
What are you gonna do?


01:31:04.917 --> 01:31:06.835
Well, I won't be working as a doorman.


01:31:11.256 --> 01:31:14.134
We'll be back
after they finish the renovations.


01:31:15.594 --> 01:31:18.305
Maybe you can join us in London
if you're interested.


01:31:19.932 --> 01:31:22.059
I know the kids
would love to see you.


01:31:22.142 --> 01:31:25.145
The kids? What about you?


01:31:48.002 --> 01:31:48.919
See?


01:31:50.129 --> 01:31:52.381
I'm one of those tough guys who can cry.


01:31:53.424 --> 01:31:54.758
Yes, you are.


01:31:56.093 --> 01:31:57.386
Yes, you are.


01:32:09.023 --> 01:32:11.442
Bye, Aunt Ali! We'll miss you.


01:32:37.750 --> 01:32:42.750
Subtitles by explosiveskull
@ subs4free.info













